  "merger_description": "Kimberly-Clark Corporation, together with its subsidiaries (**Kimberly-Clark**) proposes to acquire Kenvue Inc. and its subsidiaries (**Kenvue**) (the\u00a0**Acquisition**).\n\nKimberly-Clark is a global corporation, headquartered in the United States, which produces and sells personal care products for personal, business and industrial use. Kimberly-Clark\u2019s brands include Huggies, Kleenex, and Viva.\n\nKenvue is a global corporation, headquartered in the United States, which produces and sells consumer healthcare products. Kenvue\u2019s brands include Band-Aid, Zyrtec and Aveeno.\n\nKimberly-Clark and Kenvue both supply feminine hygiene (period care) products in Australia, namely tampons, sanitary pads and panty liners under the brands \u2018U by Kotex\u2019 (Kimberly-Clark) and \u2018Carefree\u2019 and \u2018Stayfree\u2019 (Kenvue).\n\nTo pre-emptively address potential competition concerns that may otherwise arise from the Acquisition due to the overlap between the parties in the supply of feminine hygiene products, Kimberly-Clark has offered an undertaking pursuant to section 87B of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010\u00a0which provides for the divestiture of\u00a0Kenvue's feminine hygiene business in Australia and New Zealand (the **Remedy Offer**).",
